{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful","id":464051,"title":"Isn't Gauru regeneration too powerful?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-31T17:29:53-07:00","id":464051,"title":"Isn't Gauru regeneration too powerful?","content":"All bashing and lethal damage cured at the beginning of the turn? Doesn't it make the players think they are invincible or at least provoke a &quot;meh&quot; feeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1960-thelinuxlich","name":"thelinuxlich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:42:07-07:00","id":464080,"title":"","content":"My group is pretty interested/enthusiastic about it (depending on which member you ask).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:43:18-07:00","id":464082,"title":"","content":"But you get what I mean right? Like epic level characters fighting CR 1 enemies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1960-thelinuxlich","name":"thelinuxlich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:44:22-07:00","id":464083,"title":"","content":"Not for me. Believe it or not, it's entirely possible to get churned into red mist by a prepared and determined group of antagonists, and this does nothing against aggravated damage from silver or magical sources. It's quite possible for your supposed invincibility to turn into you getting ground to mush under withering fire.<br /> <br /> This aside, though, a big part of the point of Gauru form <i>is</i> to feel invincible; like you are the Big Motherfucking Wolf Daddy(/Mommy/Alternate Gendered Parental Name). You are not some simpering mortal, you are the offspring of Mother Moon and Father Wolf; you are flesh and spirit in one with five kinds of Pissed Off surging through your veins. While it is possible for the prepared and skilled to fight against such a beast, your average mortal should dutifully piss their respective garments at the sight of you.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, they might feel invincible, but that's a part of the point - and something they're easily disabused of. If they feel &quot;Meh&quot;, though, someone, somewhere, has failed... And it might be them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:45:16-07:00","id":464085,"title":"","content":"No. But it's not meant to be used against a random drunk with a BB gun. Many of the antagonists of Werewolf are very powerful and very lethal, or come in swarms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:46:58-07:00","id":464089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thelinuxlich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful?p=464082#post464082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But you get what I mean right? Like epic level characters fighting CR 1 enemies</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really got that feel from it, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:48:36-07:00","id":464090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thelinuxlich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful#post464051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All bashing and lethal damage cured at the beginning of the turn? Doesn't it make the players think they are invincible or at least provoke a &quot;meh&quot; feeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not if you present them with a pack of degenerate Predator Kings that would eat their dead bodies, but that's not a pre-requisite.<br /> <br /> Or a Hunter in Darkness Elodoth who sneaks upon them and triggers their Death Rage in the worst situations, with none being the wiser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:08:09-07:00","id":464110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thelinuxlich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful#post464051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All bashing and lethal damage cured at the beginning of the turn? Doesn't it make the players think they are invincible or at least provoke a &quot;meh&quot; feeling?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the point! Feeling invincible doesn't mean you <i>are</i> invincible.<br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> Oh, and Gauru is not epic level; give me, say, 10 levels. Still overkill on CR 1, but that's the point.<br /> <br /> It ain't overkill against the CR 8+ enemies they be facing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":1170,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","user":"amechra","date":". 03-31-2015, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T18:08:54-07:00","id":464112,"title":"","content":"My group has had a ton of fun with it. Some of the non rahu pack members have used it to get some violence done when he was busy elsewhere, and we have had a couple giant epic fights in which Garou regeneration combined with bonus stamina from Crimson Spasm was the only reason that I survived past the first round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3347-wild-eyes","name":"Wild-Eyes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T23:31:36-07:00","id":464338,"title":"","content":"No, I haven't found any problems with it. It's powerful, sure, but even in the killing form one has to be careful. There are lots of things that can deal horrendous amounts of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T02:08:04-07:00","id":464421,"title":"","content":"The only time it can feel boring is when two Gauru are simultaneously trading blows. It becomes tactically important for your pack to harass the enemy into going Gauru first, because whoever goes Gauru second is probably going to win, unless they considerably outclass you. It also encourages actual pack tactics, such as tearing down Gauru defenses to score that precious aggravated damage without resorting to cannibalism.<br /> <br /> But you have to walk a razor's edge, because too much aggravated tempts the enemy to fall into Death Rage. And if there is anything you love and need to protect around, then you may have to make some very hard choices. Also, Predator's Unmatched Pursuit is a <i><b>bitch</b></i> because it <i><b>forces</b></i> those hard choices. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T02:34:12-07:00","id":464431,"title":"","content":"It is not so bad, really. When your pack is up against a dedicated group of antagonist, they might only need to focus attacks for a single turn before you have the first wrapped-over Aggravated damage and its only downhill from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T03:23:23-07:00","id":464487,"title":"","content":"If a bunch of young upstart werewolves are feeling invincible it is your duty as a storyteller to <i>PROVE THEM WRONG</i>. *Evil Cackle*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T03:30:51-07:00","id":464491,"title":"","content":"As I've written elsewhere, playtests included a starting pack vs pack fight where two Uratha were dead after a couple of rounds despite the use of Gauru and one of the dead werewolves being a Gauru 'specialist'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T04:06:49-07:00","id":464499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful?p=464491#post464491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I've written elsewhere, playtests included a starting pack vs pack fight where two Uratha were dead after a couple of rounds despite the use of Gauru and one of the dead werewolves being a Gauru 'specialist'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen you repeat this, but how exactly did they die? What killed them and what were the rolls looking like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T04:15:07-07:00","id":464501,"title":"","content":"I gave some more details on an earlier thread; I'll go hunting for it in a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T04:18:55-07:00","id":464503,"title":"","content":"Found it, quoting below:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well, just to start with the tale of the two dead Uratha. Turns out it was actually three turns, not two.<br /> <br /> So, the four Forsaken of the pack versus four fairly new Pure. The Pure have something to prove, heard of the new Forsaken pack and came in to try and provoke a fight with them by going for their Locus. Their aim was to steal Essence, have a brawl, hopefully beat up the Forsaken a bit and prove their dominance. The PCs, for their part, have pretty much the same idea but from the other side - they want to wound the Pure and drive them off.<br /> <br /> The actual tactics they went for, though, caused the whole thing to turn into a bloody clusterfuck.<br /> <br /> The Pure characters are slightly more combat-tuned than the PCs - most of them have honed a form (usually Urshul) and their natural weapons, and have slightly more Gifts. The mainline fighter has buffed his Stamina in Gauru form and has some appropriate fighting style dots (the one focused on all-out assaults, iirc). That said, they're also built more on thematics than optimisation so the pack leader, for example, has some stuff around using Urhan a lot for ambushes. The PCs themselves are fairly normal starting characters, with every Auspice apart from an elodoth present.<br /> <br /> How it goes down is that, rather than lots of posturing, choosing targets to spread damage around and generally beat the other side up in a healable fashion, the PCs decide to focus fire and take down the person they believe to be the most dangerous target - the Gauru specialist. Legit thinking, but completely taking a werewolf out of the fight like that - especially someone they know is focused on being the heavy hitter and Gauru-user - generally involves <i>killing</i> them.<br /> <br /> As such, when the battle starts, the Pure initially think it's a regular 'I'm harder than you and I'm going to show it' fight, but the player characters all dogpile one victim, the Gauru specialist. He flicks to Gauru asap, but the sheer volume of damage rolling in from four attackers is too much - especially the Rahu whose 8-again kicks in nicely and, more worryingly, the ambush from the Irraka. The Pure try to shift their own tactics and pile damage on the Irraka, who was already carrying a little bit of Aggravated from an earlier encounter.<br /> <br /> Both sides are lugging various arm and leg wracks at this point from the Urshul form attacks.<br /> <br /> Round 2, both the Gauru specialist and the Irraka get the crap pounded out of them The Irraka flicks to Gauru but it's too slow versus the pile-up of damage he's taking, including a fair amount of Aggravated before he ever hits the killing form; the Gauru specialist just gets severely injured despite the full health-track clearance of Lethal he's had for two turns. The Rahu also flicks to Gauru to help speed the killing.<br /> <br /> Round 3, both the Irraka and the Gauru specialist die.<br /> <br /> After this, both sides have also wounded the survivors of the other enough that more people could well die or be maimed unless (or even if) they all hit the killing form. Both sides realise this has already gone far further than they ever wanted it to, and the Forsaken allow the Pure to recover the body of their dead packmate and retreat. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T04:44:07-07:00","id":464551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful?p=464431#post464431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is not so bad, really. When your pack is up against a dedicated group of antagonist, they might only need to focus attacks for a single turn before you have the first wrapped-over Aggravated damage and its only downhill from there.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also there's always the liklihood that any earthly antagonist (human hunters, Claimed, vampires that don't like you moving in on their hunting grounds) that knows they're going to fight Werewolves is going to bring silver. I mean, why the hell wouldn't they? The only antagonist type with an incentive not to are the Pure, and their prone to ignore that with their cycle of sin and attonement (not sure how that's going to be handled in 2E, we'll see).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T07:01:32-07:00","id":464644,"title":"","content":"The only time Garou should be a &quot;problem&quot; is in one versus one fights, which Werewolf isn't particularly geared for anyways. If you're staring down a Garou in a one vs one fight with no silver then, besides reflecting on the life choices that brought you to this situation you should run and wait out the pretty short Garou timer. If they death rage, you keep running and attack them near something they aren't willing to destroy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T22:05:29-07:00","id":465659,"title":"","content":"Is there anything a werewolf in kuruth isn't willing to destroy to get at its prey (other than another 'raging packmate)? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If you play/ed using the default 1st edition rules for the gauru form and you'll appreciate the changes that were made. It still had a short timer and wasn't significantly stronger than urshul ,which became the chosen fighting form for everyone I knew (and most of the forum members I've spoken with in the past) who didn't get Primal Form. I was surprised by the number of people that didn't get that Gift. It just seems like it would be a very obvious choice given the default setting. If I knew the Pure were gunning for me I'd prefer to be able become a 9' at the shoulder Dire Wolf rather than not. It also is now easier to actually kill some of the things werewolves face, like Spirits, which was pretty much impossible without a lot of planning and some luck in 1st ed.<br /> <br /> Yes, I'm a fan of the changes. I've been playing WW since Apocalypse 1st ed so the restructuring of how Gifts work is taking a little getting used to but I very much like how renown now interacts with Gifts, I'm a bigger fan of the changes made to the different form abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T21:39:09-07:00","id":469164,"title":"","content":"The 2e games are a lot less &quot;Mundane solutions work for supernatural problems&quot; weaknesses really matter now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:34:49-07:00","id":474403,"title":"","content":"Our last session had a face-down between 3 werewolves and a wolf-blooded on one side, and about six or seven Rank 1 and 2 spirits on the other. One werewolf got so badly clobbered he never even had a chance to go into Gauru before he got KO'd, and the Rahu desperately needed every ounce of advantage Gauru gave him to hold out during the fight - plus he nearly ended up Death Raging due to a horrible combo of Conditions and Tilts he was hit with. At the end, the surviving spirits and the battered pack both retreated. The pack are needing some time to heal from the Aggravated damage that some members racked up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:51:03-07:00","id":474420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/464051-isn-t-gauru-regeneration-too-powerful?p=474403#post474403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our last session had a face-down between 3 werewolves and a wolf-blooded on one side, and about six or seven Rank 1 and 2 spirits on the other. One werewolf got so badly clobbered he never even had a chance to go into Gauru before he got KO'd, and the Rahu desperately needed every ounce of advantage Gauru gave him to hold out during the fight - plus he nearly ended up Death Raging due to a horrible combo of Conditions and Tilts he was hit with. At the end, the surviving spirits and the battered pack both retreated. The pack are needing some time to heal from the Aggravated damage that some members racked up.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good to know. While six or seven is kindof a lot, I had been filing away Rank 1 and 2 spirits as &quot;not too big of a threat&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}